  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nToday and tonight, the flow aloft will transition from an upper \nridge to SW flow aloft across Montana. Meanwhile, an upper trough\nmove into the Canadian Rockies and Pacific NW. The pattern change \nwill lead to increasing daily chances for showers and thunderstorms,\nwith heavy rain potential as some southwestern monsoonal moisture\ndoes transport its way this far north. \n\nThere will be chances for showers and thunderstorms at times\ntoday. Chances for showers and thunderstorms increase tonight  \nwith widespread rain expected between Thursday, Thursday night and\nFriday morning with heavy rain possible at times. The current\nprobability for one inch or more rain between tonight and Friday\nis 40 - 90 percent across NE Montana with higher confidence the\nmore east you go. The probability for 2 or more inches of rain \nbetween tonight and Friday is between 10 and 50 percent,\nespecially east of Fort Peck Lake. If more than 2 inches of rain \noccurs, flooding could become a possibility depending on how \nquickly the rain falls in a given location. A marginal risk of \nexcessive rainfall for NE Montana today, and a slight risk\nThursday, and another marginal for Friday. Will hold off on any \nFlood Watches for now given that the ground is dry and rainfall \nhas been light over the last 4 weeks. \n\nFlow aloft Friday night and Saturday turns into a drier WSW aloft\nas the upper trough moves east across the Canadian Prairies.\nRain chances diminish Friday afternoon and Friday night and\nSaturday look mainly dry with isolated showers possible. \n\nFrequent waves moving across eastern Montana will bring shower and\nthunderstorm chances at times early next week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nIncreased PoPs for the first 8 hours to better capture AM showers.\nNo changes to NBM otherwise.\n\nLow confidence in shower and thunderstorm chances today. Confidence\nin precipitation chances increase tonight and Thursday and are\nhigh Thursday night and Friday morning. High confidence in many\nareas getting an inch or more rain overall but low confidence\npossibility of amounts higher than an inch.",
